1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,348
Technical hiring should reveal how someone thinks—

2
00:00:03,388 --> 00:00:06,236
not just how well they answer a list of questions.

3
00:00:06,276 --> 00:00:07,853
Meet Autonomous Interviewer.

4
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:11,522
Sarah is interviewing for a Senior Data Engineer role.

5
00:00:11,562 --> 00:00:15,504
She explains how she would monitor an LLM-powered production system,

6
00:00:15,544 --> 00:00:19,954
covering latency, tokens, failures, retrieval, tools, and trace correlation.

7
00:00:19,994 --> 00:00:23,877
The interviewer understands her answer and immediately goes deeper.

8
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:27,772
This is where Autonomous Interviewer is different.

9
00:00:27,812 --> 00:00:30,195
It does not simply move to the next question.

10
00:00:30,235 --> 00:00:32,079
When Sarah makes a technical claim,

11
00:00:32,119 --> 00:00:35,686
the system decides whether that claim should be tested in practice.

12
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:39,370
The interviewer introduces a focused coding exercise

13
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:43,344
built around the conversation: instrument a production function.

14
00:00:43,384 --> 00:00:46,263
Sarah implements the solution, runs the checks,

15
00:00:46,303 --> 00:00:48,313
and passes all four requirements.

16
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,752
That implementation does not disappear into a coding editor.

17
00:00:52,792 --> 00:00:55,343
It becomes structured interview evidence—

18
00:00:55,383 --> 00:00:57,998
connected to the rest of the conversation.

19
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:01,298
The interview continues from that evidence.

20
00:01:01,338 --> 00:01:04,813
Sarah explains how she would handle structured events,

21
00:01:04,853 --> 00:01:08,327
trace IDs, retries, failures, and performance signals.

22
00:01:08,367 --> 00:01:13,338
The system keeps the discussion focused on what still needs to be understood.

23
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:34,833
Then the conversation becomes a hiring-ready assessment.

24
00:01:34,873 --> 00:01:37,588
The assessor sees what Sarah demonstrated,

25
00:01:37,628 --> 00:01:40,934
what she implemented, where the evidence is strong,

26
00:01:40,974 --> 00:01:42,967
and what still needs follow-up.

27
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:46,374
Autonomous Interviewer turns a technical conversation

28
00:01:46,414 --> 00:01:48,820
into practical, evidence-backed evaluation.

29
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:52,313
Not an AI that simply asks interview questions.

30
00:01:52,353 --> 00:01:55,651
An interviewer that decides what it needs to know next.

